  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 42a7ef911f4c60e408989a759d2b9b18, type: 3}
  m_Name: PHP_BOOLEAN
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CodeEscape.Programming.LessonData
  id: PHP_BOOLEAN
  language: 2
  conceptTitle: 'Boolean Logic: &&, || and !'
  symbol: '&&'
  relatedQuestionIds:
  - PHP_06_BOOLEAN
  topics:
  - Boolean Logic
  definition: Boolean logic works with the values true and false. It lets a program
    combine several conditions into one answer.
  howItWorks: '&& (AND) is true only when both sides are true. || (OR) is true when
    at least one side is true. ! (NOT) flips a value: !true is false. Work out !
    first, then &&, then ||.'
  exampleCode: '<?php

    $raining = true;

    $umbrella = false;

    $dry = !$raining
    && $umbrella;

    $wet = $raining || $umbrella;

    ?>'
  exampleExplanation: '!$raining flips true to false, and && needs both sides to
    be true, so $dry is false. || only needs one true side: $raining is true, so
    $wet is true.'
  tip: For &&, check both sides. For ||, one true side is enough.
